messages:    1%|          | 2/204 [00:00<00:17, 11.88it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James either takes the database course or has a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "James either takes the database course or has a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain, let\'s analyze the given information step by step:.\n\n1.**No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This means that if James works in the library, he cannot be from the computer science department.\n\n2.**All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.**.\n   - This implies that if James has a part-time job offered by the university, he must work in the library.\n\n3.**All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This means that if James takes the database course, he must be from the computer science department.\n\n4.**All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**.\n   - This implies that if James is instructed by professor David, he must be taking the database course.\n\n5.**All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.**.\n   - This means that if James works in the lab, he must be instructed by professor David.\n\n6.**James is a student working in the lab.**.\n   - This tells us that James works in the lab.\n\nJack both has a part-time job offered by the university and works in the lab.\n   - This tells us that Jack has a part-time job offered by the university and works in the lab.\n\nNow, let\'s apply this information to James:.\n\n- Since James does not work in the lab, he must not be instructed by professor David.\n- Since James is not instructed by professor David, he must not be taking the database course.\n- Since James is not taking the database course, he must not be from the computer science department.\n- Since James is not from the computer science department, he must be from the computer science department (from point 1, which contradicts our previous conclusion).\n\nGiven the contradiction, we can definitively determine that James does not take the database course or have a part-time job offered by the university based on the provided information. Therefore, the statement "James either takes the database course or has a part-time job offered by the university" is certain.\n\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
