messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\n[BG] Books contain tons of knowledge. [BG] When a person reads a book, that person gains knowledge. [BG] If a person gains knowledge, they become smarter. Harry read the book “Walden” by Henry Thoreau.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Harry is smarter than before.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Harry is smarter than before" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, let\'s break down the information step by step:.\n\n1.**Context Analysis**:.\n   - Books contain tons of knowledge.\n   - Reading a book allows a person to gain knowledge.\n   - Gaining knowledge makes a person smarter.\n   - Harry read the book "Walden" by Henry Thoreau.\n\n2.**Logical Steps**:.\n   - Since Harry read the book "Walden," he gained knowledge.\n   - Losing knowledge makes Harry dumber.\n   - Therefore, Harry is dumber than before.\n\n3.**Conclusion**:.\n   - Based on the logical steps, the statement "Harry is dumber than before" is true.\n\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
