hen they do not go to bed late and wake up every day after noon.\n   - Remy either both goes to bed late and wakes up every day after noon and spends their free time tidying and organizing the spaces in their home, or they do not go to bed late and wake up every day after noon nor spend their free time tidying and organizing the spaces in their home.\n\n2.**Identify Relevant Information**:.\n   - The relevant information for determining if Remy visits the office supply store regularly is the third bullet point: "All people who work regularly and often at home visit the office supply store regularly.".\n\n3.**Apply the Information**:.\n   - Since Remy either spends their free time tidying and organizing the spaces in their home or does not, and the third bullet point states that all people who work regularly and often at home visit the office supply store regularly, we need to consider both scenarios:.\n     - If Remy spends their free time tidying and organizing the spaces in their home, then they do not go to bed late and wake up every day after noon.This means they are working regularly and often at home, so they would visit the office supply store regularly.If Remy spends their free time tidying and organizing the spaces in their home, then they go to bed late and wake up every day after noon. This means they are working regularly and often at home, so they would visit the office supply store regularly.\n\n4.**Conclusion**:.\n- The statement "Remy visits the office supply store regularly" is certain because it depends on whether Remy spends their free time tidying and organizing the spaces in their home or not. If they do, they wouldn\'t visit the office supply store regularly; if they don\'t, they would.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:.\nB) Certain.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
