messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people perform in school talent shows often, then they attend and are very engaged with school events. People either perform in school talent shows often or are inactive and disinterested members of their community. If people chaperone high school dances, then they are not students who attend the school. All people who are inactive and disinterested members of their community chaperone high school dances. All young children and teenagers who wish to further their academic careers and educational opportunities are students who attend the school. Bonnie either both attends and is very engaged with school events and is a student who attends the school, or she neither attends and is very engaged with school events nor is a student who attends the school.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? If Bonnie is either both a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities and chaperones high school dances or neither is a young child nor teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities, then Bonnie is either a student who attends the school or is an inactive and disinterested member of the community.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', "<think>.\nTo determine the truth value of the given statement, let's break down the information provided and analyze it step by step:.\n\n1.**Context Analysis**:.\n   - People who perform in school talent shows often are engaged with school events.\n   - People who are inactive and disinterested members of their community do not perform in school talent shows often.\n   - People who chaperone high school dances are not students who attend the school.\n   - All inactive and disinterested members of the community chaperone high school dances.\n   - Young children and teenagers who wish to further their academic careers and educational opportunities are students who attend the school.\n\n2.**Given Statement**:.\n   - If Bonnie is either both a young child or teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities and chaperones high school dances or neither is a young child nor teenager who wishes to further her academic career and educational opportunities, then Bonnie is either a student who attends the school or is an inactive and disinterested member of the community.\n\n3.**Reasoning**:.\n   - We need to check if the given statement logically follows from the context.\n   - The context states that performing in school talent shows often indicates engagement with school events.\n   - Chaperoning high school dances indicates that someone is not a student who attends the school.\n   - Inactive and disinterested members of the community chaperone high school dances.Old adults and elderly individuals who have no interest in advancing their academic careers and educational opportunities are not students who attend the school.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
