messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nOn some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV. Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor. Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people. All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows. Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Breaking Bad is a TV show in which roses are given out on Monday at 8 pm.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Breaking Bad is a TV show in which roses are given out on Monday at 8 pm" is true, false, or uncertain, let\'s break down the given information step by step:.\n\n1.**Context Analysis**:.\n   - On some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV.\n   - Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor.\n   - Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people.\n   - All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows.\n   - Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n2.**Statement Breakdown**:.\n   - The statement claims that Breaking Bad is a TV show where roses are given out on Monday at 8 pm.\n\n3.**Reasoning**:.\n   - From the context, we know that roses are given out on TV on some Mondays at 8 pm.\n   - The Bachelor is a show where roses are given out on TV.\n   - Since the Bachelor is a show where roses are given out on TV, and it is a reality TV show (as it portrays the lives of real people), it follows that roses are indeed given out on TV on some Mondays at 8 pm.Therefore, the incorrect answer is:\nA) Certain.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
