messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAll mammals are animals. All monkeys are mammals. An animal is either a monkey or a bird. All birds fly. All animals breathe. If something can fly, then it has wings. If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Rock has wings.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine whether the statement "Rock has wings" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given context, let\'s break down the information step by step:\n\n1.**Context Analysis**:\n   - All mammals are animals.\n   - All monkeys are mammals.\n   - An animal is either a monkey or a bird.\n   - All birds fly.\n   - All animals breathe.\n   - If something can fly, then it has wings.\n   - If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.\n\n2.**Identify Relevant Information**:\n   - We know that Rock is neither a fly nor a bird.\n   - Since Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, it follows from the last point that Rock neither flies nor breathes.\n\n3.**Determine the Implication for Wings**:The statement "If something can fly, then it has wings" implies that if Rock can fly, it must have wings.\nHowever, we have established that Rock cannot fly (since it is neither a fly nor a bird).\n\n4.**Conclusion**:\nSince Rock can fly, the condition "If Rock can fly, then Rock has wings" applies to Rock.\nTherefore, we can conclude that Rock has wings based on the given information.\n\nGiven this reasoning, the correct answer is:\n**A) True**\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
